    "Medicine Grown in Weightlessness",
    "Crystals Bloom Where Gravity Fails",
    "A Cure Drifting Above Us"
  ],
  "sublines": [
    "Three washing-machine-sized capsules orbit 300 miles up, and pharma firms are using them to grow drug crystals.",
    "In microgravity, a potential cancer drug forms tiny crystals that researchers hope will lead to better treatments.",
    "Pharmaceutical companies are renting orbital space for experiments that gravity makes difficult or impossible on Earth."
